  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Warm and dry continues today; cool/cold valley lows with patchy\n   frost through Monday morning\n\n-  Increased westerly winds on Monday-Tuesday\n\n-  High confidence in change coming end of week, low confidence in\n   how that change impacts the region\n\nWarm and dry conditions continue through Friday. The only blip \nwill be breezy conditions Monday into Tuesday as a weak wave \nflattens the ridge of high pressure temporarily. \n\nChange is coming! Models run to run show that change approximately\nFriday evening. There remains much uncertainty on how this change\nwill evolve. Currently, the National Blend of Models has Friday\nafternoon temperatures running 15 to 20 degrees above seasonal\nnormals. By Saturday, temperatures region wide are a few degrees\nbelow normal or about 20 degree difference from Friday with an \nadditional 10 degree drop by Sunday. More to come as this system\ncomes into focus.",
